Hmm, perhaps a new use for an old item is in order.

YANI:  tin openers + starting pets

If you have a tame cat or dog, using a tin opener acts as a magic
whistle.

This isn't terribly overbalanced, because it requires that
a) you haven't polymorphed your pet into something stronger, or gotten
a new one.
b) you have a tin opener - a relatively useless item, in addition to
being rare
c) you have a tin - these are hard to find in the early game.

Basically, this makes the game slightly easier for beginning characters
without changing the difficulty for mid- to late-game.  It ensures that
you know where your cat or dog are, as long as you happen to come
across this particular combination of items.

